<title>MEXICO: Mexico's Ortiz sees US interest rates to rise.</title>
<headline>Mexico's Ortiz sees US interest rates to rise.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican Finance Minister Guillermo Ortiz said in an interview published on Tuesday that he estimated key U.S. interest rates will rise between 0.75 and 1.00 percentage point in what remains of the year.</p>
<p>Ortiz told the daily El Financiero his estimation was based on the U.S. &quot;strategy to continue deflating the New York Stock Exchange&quot;.</p>
</text>
